\ Output-type propagation: `fib` declares a fixnum result, so the caller
\ narrows the returned value at the call site (tag check plus unbox) and the
\ following `inspect` sees a proven fixnum and monomorphizes. Under the lock
\ any interpreter fallback of any category rejects the build, so a successful
\ build is itself the proof that a computed value carries its declared type
\ across the call.
\
\ The parameter side needs no annotations: call-site inference proves them.

fib-step: ( a b n -- result ) [ dup 0 = [ drop drop ] [ 1 - [ swap over + ] dip fib-step ] if ] ;
fib: ( n -- result: fixnum ) [ dup 2 < [ ] [ 0 1 <rot- fib-step ] if ] ;

30 fib inspect print-line
